SUMMARY:Walk Connemara (Carl Sandburg's Home) and the Village of Flat Rock
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nSpend time on the treelin
 ed trails walked by Carl Sandburg. Walk around a lake\, past his home\, by
  the goat barn\, and over the rock where Sandburg often wrote his poetry. 
 Then walk a short distance to visit the quaint shops of the village of Fla
 t Rock. Go by the rock for which the village is named and past the Flat Ro
 ck Playhouse (the official NC State Playhouse).\n\nThe trees are changing 
 colors. There are several views of beautiful Fall panoramas. You can stop 
 and watch the baby goats play as their mothers watch on.\n\nWe will be wal
 king with the Asheville Amblers Walking Club\, AARP\, Strider\, and perhap
 s some others. We will register in the back parking lot at **Quality Inn &
  Suites Hendersonville - Flat Rock\, 111 Commercial Blvd.\, Flat Rock NC 2
 8731**\, at the I-26 exit 53 (next to Cracker Barrel). Be there at 9:30 sh
 arp\, as we have to travel from there to the Start Point\, trying for a 10
 :00 step-off\, or as soon as possible after 10. Don't worry\, we will give
  you simple directions to get to the Start Point.\n\nThere will be 5 KM/3 
 mile and 10 KM/6 mile options. The 5 KM walk is described in the first par
 agraph above. Sandburg used to like to climb Big Glassy Mountain on his pr
 operty\, and that is the additional distance for the 10 KM walk. It is a n
 ice trail\, but fairly steep. The view from the top of Big Glassy is defin
 itely worth the effort.\n\nThis is a hilly walk\, even if you don't do Big
  Glassy\; many will want walking poles. A portion of the trail has roots a
 nd other tripping hazards. Tennis shoes will be fine for most\; if it has 
 rained that day there is one slick place\, so be sure your shoes have good
  tread. Bring a protein snack and water bottle. Dogs on leash are acceptab
 le\, but are unable to go into the buildings on the Connemara property. St
 rollers are not recommended.\n\nThere are restrooms near the beginning of 
 the walk and near the Sandburg house.\n\nIn the Village of Flat Rock there
  is a great BBQ place where some of our group will have lunch.
