SUMMARY:Walk Biltmore Estate's Deer Park Trail on Bittersweet Chocolate w/
 Almonds Day
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nTravel past the Biltmore 
 House toward Antler Hill Village. Park in the first available area on the 
 left just past the Lagoon. We will access the Deer Park Trail from there. 
 (I will be monitoring the Comments section of this walk page and also Meet
 up messages. If you get confused or lost\, contact me right away.)\n\nDeer
  Park Trail goes through the Deer Park (though it isn't near Lioncrest and
  the other DeerPark facilities). It comes to a T intersection. We will go 
 right to where you can access the Garden Trails. Then we will turn around 
 and go up the hill to the South Terrace of the Biltmore House. From there 
 we will retrace our steps to the start point. It is about 2.5 miles round 
 trip\, or so says the map.\n\nI've done this walk in both tennis shoes and
  in light hiking boots (from a different start point). I'll probably bring
  walking poles for the hill\, though most of the walk won't need them.\n\n
 Bring plenty of water and a protein snack. Dress for the weather\; conside
 r a hat and sunscreen. Dogs are welcome. Trail strollers would probably wo
 rk.\n\nPS: It being National Bittersweet Chocolate with Almonds Day\, we j
 ust might enjoy some at the end of the walk!!
